// RFC 6582's guard, and the loss state's resends: two segments of 988, the first resent by the timeout at +0.2. The
// timeout marks both lost, records recover = 1976, the last byte sent, sets the target max(1976 / 2, 2 * 988) = 1976
// and restarts the window at what is in flight after the marking, nothing, plus one segment, which the head's resend
// fills. Three duplicates then acknowledge 1, which does not cover more than recover: they begin no recovery, and
// after a timeout a duplicate takes nothing out of what is in flight either, so nothing leaves. The ACK of the head,
// a tenth of a second later so that an earlier resend would fail the line, is short of recover: slow start doubles
// the window and the second segment, marked at the timeout, leaves at once. The ACK of both ends the loss state.
// Linux stays in its loss state until the same ACK and resends the second segment on the first ACK of new data as
// well (tcp_process_loss).
--congestion=newreno
0 socket(..., SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_TCP) = 3
+0 bind(3, ..., ...) = 0
+0 listen(3, 1) = 0

+0 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1000,nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 0>
+0 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,nop,nop,TS val 0 ecr 100>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 0>
+0 accept(3, ..., ...) = 4

+0 write(4, ..., 1976) = 1976
+0 > P. 1:989(988) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 0 ecr 100>
+0 > P. 989:1977(988) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 0 ecr 100>
+0.2 > P. 1:989(988) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 200 ecr 100>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 200>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 200>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 200>
+0.1 < . 1:1(0) ack 989 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 200>
+0 > P. 989:1977(988) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 300 ecr 100>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1977 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 300>
+2 close(4) = 0
+0 > F. 1977:1977(0) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 2300 ecr 100>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1978 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 2300>
